Description: Save a prefix cache snapshot at the start of the last user message too.
 The prefix cache saved a snapshot at the end of the system prompt and tools, and one at the end of each prompt. A new
 prompt resumes only from a snapshot whose tokens begin it, because the recurrent state of Qwen3.5, Qwen3.6 and Qwen3.8
 cannot be rewound to an earlier position. Prompts which share everything but their last user message, like the same
 few-shot examples followed by different inputs, or the same document followed by different questions, therefore
 shared only the system prompt, and only when it was at least 512 tokens long, and every prompt read the shared history
 again.
 .
 The history before the last user message is now saved as well, as a boundary snapshot, when the prompt before shared
 it and went on with another last message, as prompts with the same few-shot examples do. Reading up to it takes a
 prefill pass of its own, which on qwen3.6-moe:35b-a3b costs about 3.5 seconds whatever its length, so a chat, whose
 every turn only continues the turn before, does not save it. It is saved when it is at least 512 tokens into the
 prompt and adds at least --prefix-min-gain tokens to the system prompt and tools and to what the prompt resumed from.
 The end snapshots saved after it hold only the rows after it. Qwen3.8, which keeps only the shared start of a
 conversation, keeps it as well.
 .
 With a short system prompt and 3,500 tokens of few-shot examples, on a Ryzen AI 9 HX 370, every prompt from the third
 one on read only its own last message, in about 5 seconds instead of 18 on qwen3.6-moe:35b-a3b and in 4.5 seconds
 instead of 33 on qwen3.8-dflash2:27b. A chat of four turns took as long as without the patch.
 .
 Two tests of the prefix cache cover a shared history and a chat.
Author: Mitar
Forwarded: no
